    36	## Where we enter
    37	
    38	It is the 270th day at Lowmarch. There are six now, with Oryn's first post-thaw stop [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 20] at Pike's plank. Lira has two arms she does not quite trust, and Brom's shoulder is still bound and unread. The ferryman says the ice will go in a week, and has said so for a week. Karis's case is made and no one has answered it.
    39	
    40	## What this movement is for
    41	
    42	The book's question arrives as paper, carried by the last man anyone expected to carry it. Vastin comes through the board with no rank, no seal and a bad knee. Over two scenes he hands over three things in an order he decided on the road. The man who brings them has nothing to do once they are on the table, and the movement makes that hurt.
    43	
    44	Consequential turns and promises:
    45	- **The week before the ferry** (270th–276th). Tents return to the meadow. Oryn's patients come to the plank, seen from outside. Teague's crew gets ready for the road after the thaw. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 20]
    46	- **Lira's return to the floor** (~2,000, learning fight). It is her first two-armed bout with Cael since the Ring. The arm tells her once and she does not stop. That is the visible correction (it pays at Millrace: "Once.").
    47	- **The ferry** (277th, first light). The river is in flood and the rope is strained, and a passenger holds a line physically, with no Path, before Cael knows the stance (~1,500). Then: "Cael knew the stance before he knew the face." "Vastin," Seln says, in the voice for an inventory. "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father."
    48	- **The plank.** Pike: "What'd he do?" / "Nothing. Out here. Nothing yet." / "Then he's nothing yet." A copper and a half for bread. Teague reads the man's hands a step longer than a crew looks. Lira's face for men in grey doesn't fit a brown coat.
    49	- **The long table** (midday). The Seln–Vastin doorway exchange, verbatim; these are their first words to each other. Vastin says the short thing: he resigned or walked out. Brom: "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." The layer: Karis supplies its existence ("Under every station on the continent. I said so at a table before we left Ostrand") [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]. Vastin's new fact: "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key." The name is a citation to a designer, and the trail ends at Treswick. Vastin then has nothing to do. Lira asks "Why us." Oryn notices the knee: "Then I still haven't asked." "What follows you": nothing that crosses the Line, and the Stair's rim "is not mine". Cael remembers the Book 6 sentence and says only, "Ask him the thing you want to ask him." Karis asks. **Close (verbatim).**
    50	- **The back room** (evening), in Vastin's order:
    51	  1. **The records.** A courier's flat holding six years of abstracts, the anomaly column ("Total"), and six rows. "More than four." The completion report is the last sheet.
    52	  2. **The page,** verbatim and set apart.
    53	  3. **The technician's sheet,** verbatim, with the bar. Karis writes *not read*. Seln goes still and does not say the sum.
    54	  
    55	  Vastin is sent to bed ("don't take the stairs fast"). Cael's hand stays a hand's width from the page. Nobody says *west*.
    56	
    57	**Physical challenge:** Lira's bout and the flood landing. The rest is pressure carried in documents.
    58	**Cutaway (~2,500):** Vastin. He walks the last miles to the Line. Three strangers tell him "go to the plank". A broker prices him at nothing. He has the page in his coat and the flat on his back. **He never computes the date on the deep-layer sheet.** He knows only the bar.
    59	**Development:** about 12 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 3, Karis 2, Seln 1–2, Brom 1, Lira 2, Oryn 1, Pike 1.
    60	
    61	## What must remain true / withheld
    62	
    63	- No Iron Wall is shown. Vastin holds the ferry line with his hands and body only.
    64	- Vastin's **age is not stated** (OWNER #17; §12 C1). "Forty years" is his own rounding. The Compact's spans of time are anchored to events, not numbers (§12 C2).
    65	- The sub-layer's existence is already Karis's knowledge. Vastin's new facts are only that **it cannot be reached**, the citation, the suppressed records, and the deep-layer line.
    66	- **Nobody connects the date to anyone.** Seln's stillness goes unexplained, and Cael does not know what it was. "Six years" is the office's rounding.
    67	- "The Architect" is a word Karis has never read in any stratum. She calls it a title, not a name, and says no more. The leaf does not appear.
    68	- Vastin does not see the directive or the objection; they are buried in the flat's last row. He does not know the integration mechanism. He does not ask to join, and nobody frames him as joining.
    69	- Seln teaches nobody yet.
    70	
    71	## What the author owns
    72	
    73	What the week's tents and patients look like. How the landing in flood goes. What Teague's crew does about the stranger. The order of who sits down at the long table, though Lira sits last. How the back room's lamp moves. The texture of Vastin's coat, stick and knee. Humour at the edges: Brom's pricing, Pike's ledger, the mule's empty chair.
    74	
    75	## Where we leave pressure
    76	
    77	A page lies on the bare end of a table with a title and a place written on it. The place is west, inside walls. Cael's hand has been near it for the length of a lamp and has not touched it. A thing that is not yet his is a thing he can still refuse, and everyone in the room knows he won't.
