    19	2. **The rope is not bought in this movement.** The first boat carries people and no goods in that water; the cordage stays on the western landing. The debt stands, and it is why the ferry has only one hauling line when she needs two.
    20	3. **The cutaway comes before the ferry**, at the end of chapter 8, headed with its day, and names him. The reader knows who is on the far bank; Cael does not.
    21	4. **The daylight hearing** that Cael promised on the 268th is staged on the 271st, and it is about the price, in the registry's own machinery. He does not rule: he will see what the first boat brings.
    22	5. **No yardage, no new ceilings.** No instrument is put in his hand. No theory is offered for anything.
