   117	
   118	- **The coordinator's two notes on Movement 1's repair arrived during the read and the draft.** Chapters 5 and 6 were re-read from disk after the first; the second came after chapter 7 was written and changed two things in it: the restriction's trigger is now stated as the locked text has it (an enrolled name written in a book inside a district; served within the hour; the man who writes the name serves the paper), and "a piece of her Path" became "a piece out of a healer's Path". No possessive pronoun stands before "Path" anywhere in the six chapters.
   119	- **Chapter 7.** The hurdle is woven on the evening of the 272nd (not the 274th), so that the chapter runs in order and the bout follows it the next morning. The scene of the price is one continuous hearing on the 271st; Cael says that he heard the case again by daylight "the day after" the fire. Seln no longer says anything that he could not know from this bank (the five bags and the kept hour of Book 6 ch58 happened after the crew had left): the paper "has found nothing yet to take hold of", and the order's hour "fell after we were gone". Pike's season figure is written but not voiced.
   120	- **Chapter 8.** The window opens "Twelve days before that boat, when the count at Lowmarch stood at two hundred and sixty-five". Added to it: the frame-house door and the second reading that he declined (allowed to the cutaway by the map's POV table; the reason is not given); a flat cake left on a stump, and a copper that is still there in the morning. The rain on the night of the 275th and Lira's arm in the wet were added to the river scene.
   121	- **Chapter 9: the straps were renamed** so that the picture holds: the scow hangs by a **bow strap** and a **stern strap**, and it is the stern strap that parts. Her stern swings downstream on the bow strap "like a gate on one hinge". The passenger takes the torn strap's tail, passes it once round the stern rail-post and behind his own back, and sits back on it. Seln drops the drum's pawl ("an iron dog"); the tall man drives the wedge and says nothing; Teague's bow and the young one put their shoulders to the beam. The crossing home takes twenty-two minutes by Hesk's clock. The scene on the landing and the scene at the plank are two scenes; the chapter has five.
   122	- **Chapter 10.** Added: Vastin asks that it be written down ("In Ostrand I asked that nothing should be written… I ask the contrary now"); the six give him their names, Seln last; the mender and the shimmed frame, told by Vastin as his reason for believing the man; why he could not go to the archive himself (a book at its door); he asks the keeper for a bed and pays a fourth coin, and Brom adds up four and a half coppers. The chapter ends on Lira's two words.
   123	- **Chapter 11.** The table runs on without a break through the first three scenes of the plan, which are here two scenes and a third; the scene breaks fall after the knee, after Vastin's statement about the pending paper, and at the boy's cry. Added: Vastin says, from the inside, what "pending jurisdiction" is (the fourteenth chapter's ninth part; it does not lapse; he could not have lifted it); "You file a thing where it can be found again." The completion report moved out of this chapter: chapter 11 ends at "More than four" and "I am counting".
   124	- **"More than four."** Karis reads the clerk's figure under *Total* and then counts for herself the different groups of four signs in one row, a finger to each; her thumb goes down last. She will not say how many more, because the clerk's figure and her count do not agree. No figure is printed.
   125	- **Chapter 12.** Opens with the last sheet. Added: what a routing note is (Seln), and the tray marked *held* (Vastin); Seln's reading of a paper that arrives without its note (somebody wished him to have it, or wished to learn what he would do), which Vastin cannot decide; Vastin says that he cut the leaf from a register and that it was wrong; Blade asks *Edge?* of the cut and is told no; Karis's receipt, printed; Seln lays down his wand at forty-seven; Oryn shuts her mouth a third time (the 268th, the 271st, tonight). The stair: he takes four steps fast, stops, and goes on slowly, and nobody below can say whether it was her order or the knee.
   126	- **Nobody says the direction's name** in chapters 10, 11 or 12, in speech. The boy's cry at the landing is "Boat's going over". Seln says that the report "went over" on the hundred and second day.
