    85	### Stagings the coordinator may want to check
    86	
    87	- **"Not that…" answers a title spoken by Cael** (`"Archmarshal," he said.` 9:181). The plan pins neither who says the title nor to whom the answer is given. Seln's "Vastin," is said low, at Cael's shoulder, to nobody on the planks, so that the doorway at noon is still those two men's first exchange.
    88	- **"What'd he do?"** is put by Pike to the six; Cael opens his mouth, shuts it, and lets Vastin answer for himself. Pike says the last line "over, to the tents" (narrated; printed once) and writes nothing.
    89	- **"Three hundred miles is a demonstration."** answers Seln, who has just named the grade of approach that begins with a man arriving with nothing. Vastin gives the distance himself at 10:91.
    90	- **"Under every station on the continent…"** breaks in on Vastin's "I asked whether it was so in our house's frames only, or—". The paragraph after it is Karis saying what she had, at the strength of Book 6 ch39 and no more ("from that same leaf, by inference, and from the three oldest papers in the case… the reading was older than the function… I entered it as a limit"). The "will not" that Vastin corrects is Lira's ("they'll not open it for you or for anybody"), with her own "that they found there" from Book 6.
    91	- **"Then I still haven't asked."** answers Vastin's "I have not come to be mended… I offer it to nobody", said before Oryn has got past "That leg—".
    92	- **"What follows you?"** is Seln's; a question mark is supplied. "is not mine" stands inside "The rim of the Stair is not mine." The place is named to him first by Lira (11:65).
    93	- **Karis's question** before the close is mine: why he did not lay three papers before a council under his own seal before he gave the seal up.
    94	- **The close's ellipsis** is one paragraph of mine (he stops; his left hand shuts; he looks at it and at none of the six).
    95	- **"More than four."** is given to Karis. She has read the clerk's figure under *Total* and then counted for herself the different groups of four signs in one row, a finger to each, the thumb last; she will not say how many more, because the clerk's figure and her own count disagree. **No number is printed for either.** If the source prints the total, one sentence at 11:241 or 11:253 changes.
    96	- **"don't take the stairs fast"** is Karis's, at the end of her order. Vastin begins to walk it back twice ("I should prefer to remain until your copy has been compared with—"; "There is the matter of the tapes—"), goes, takes four steps fast, stops, and climbs the rest slowly; Brom says that it was the knee. I kept it open on purpose, so that BOOK_MAP §13's lock (no order taken without walking it back before Millrace) holds.
    97	- **The Book 6 sentence** is narrated, not printed (11:95): "that he had known a thing to be imperfect, and had not known that it was meant to be."
    98	- **"Nobody says *west*."** Nobody says it in speech in chapters 10–12. The narration says "the word for where the town lay" (12:219). In chapter 9 the narration has "to the west" once, of the far bank (9:67).
    99	- **Seln's stillness** is at the date (12:139–147); he says "I have read it", which is true. Cael looks at the date himself and cannot turn it into days. Nobody connects it to anything.
   100	- **"A classification event"** is defined by Vastin as "any occasion upon which a person is classed. A Kindling is one. So is a rank confirmed, or a second reading. There are some thousands of them in a year." (12:125). If the plan would rather the phrase went unexplained on this night, it is one speech.
