editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/manuscript/chapter-26.md:253:Then she smiled, the real smile, not the one she spent on strangers or on Marrow, and it reached her eyes and stayed. She knocked her shoulder against his, lightly, the left one, the Renn one, which did not hurt any more. "And it was a good fight. Leave the rest aside a minute. You worked well tonight, Cael. You didn't waste a day of those two weeks."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-58.md:43:He reached across the table to where a copy of the challenge lay, the three pages Coss had set on Naveth's blotter on the Monday of the nineteenth week. Quenna had laid it at his elbow that morning without a word. He turned to the first page and found the line with his finger.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-42.md:5:It was the middle of the morning on the Monday of the nineteenth week, between the second bell and the third, and the yard was full of the ordinary traffic of a school between lectures. Students crossed with books under their arms and kit over their shoulders, a cart of flour sacks was being checked in at the kitchen gate, and a second-year was being shouted at by somebody for leaving a door open. Cael was sitting on the low step of the lecture wing with the observation notebook on his knee, halfway down a page about Edran's off arm. He had watched the third structure come up whole four times in five that morning at the high windows, and he was trying to write down why, when something at the gate pulled his eyes off the page as a wrong note pulls a listener's head round.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-42.md:125:"Here's how it will go," she said, "so we don't waste a day of it pretending. It'll be the assembly room, on the ground floor of the lecture wing. The record's public, every word. Our counsel gets to see their documents on a timetable, and they get to see ours. Either side can enter witnesses of fact, by name." She counted the points off on her fingers, as Lira counted rumors. "Counsel will fight the timetable and the scope and the order of documents, and every one of those fights buys us days. None of them buys us the result. He went straight for the wording that sheltered you. That means he read our file as carefully as I wrote it."
