editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-28.md:119:Karis, when he found her in carrel eleven the next morning, did not wait for him to finish, and by noon she had a box: a plain pasteboard document box from the stationer's in Ostrand. Into it, in order, went every sheet the provision had ever produced about him: the enrollment record, Gault's baseline note, every drill sheet he had built and every countersignature on each, every floor issue, wrong and revised, every supervised hour since his first week on the bluff. Each was copied in her small hand where the original could not leave the wing, and each copy was dated and initialled and cross-referenced to the original's place in the wing's own files.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-27.md:221:The nine fragments lay in him where they had lain since a ford. He was sure of that as well. When Lira's hand went up, Wind had leaned in his own feet to go with hers, as it had leaned every day for two years, and he had put it down without thinking; and that had been on the far side of where the stone now stood. Anchor was asking about the stone already. *There?*
