editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/manuscript/chapter-12.md:59:Near the top of the lane they passed the gate of the yard where the woman had worked on her shoulder. She was not there, but the old man was, in his corner in the shade, set in the same stance as if he had not moved since the day before, and as they went by his pale eyes came round to Cael, then to Lira's canvas roll, then to the way the lane ran on toward the Cinder House.
