   161	## State at movement end (for the ledger)
   162	
   163	**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and seventy-seventh day past the Line**, at Lowmarch. Days on the page: 271, 272, 273, 275, 276, 277; Vastin's window, 265–276. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page.
   164	
   165	**Where everyone is.** Seven under the lower inn's roof: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln; Oryn, who is on her road and at her bench by first light; and **Vastin, in the loft over the tap, at a copper a night**, who is on nobody's sheet and has asked for nothing but a bed. Teague's five are at the upper inn, with forty sacks of salt on the bank. The brown mule is in the ferryman's shed.
   166	
   167	**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: thirty** (the read on the ground at the landing, the 277th). Shadow used twice in all and shut; held at dusk on the 272nd and the 277th. Anchor's counted uses still two. Tide: Oryn twice, himself three times, nobody else; he did not ask to read the knee. **The still place** has not been read, touched or named. He has not touched the cord or either brass edge for a hundred and nine days; the ruling is *hold*. His near sight went at the landing and was back for print by the afternoon. **He has not ruled.** He said on the 271st that he would rule when the first boat was in, and on the night of the 277th that he would say it "at the plank in the morning, in daylight" and ask for hands. He has not touched the leaf; his hand lay a hand's width from it for the whole of a lamp. He lost the bout to Lira, two touches to three. He has written to Ephram. He kept back his own question to Vastin (why the second reading was declined) and does not know the answer. He has told Vastin nothing of what he carries.
   168	
   169	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Left arm: the eighth day out of the wool on the 273rd. It told her once, in the bout, and she did not stop.** It is slow; she has woven a hurdle with it, tied a trace with both hands, and been pulled to her feet by it; it ached after rain. She did not fall on it. Right ankle sound in the great boot. Her certificate is in her coat; she does not know any longer what she would be holding it for. She still has Oryn's crossbow and its one bolt (not mentioned in these chapters). She sat last at the table and asked "Why us."
   170	
   171	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No declaration; no grey at the landing. **Right shoulder still in the older healer's webbing**; she pressed the knot on the 272nd and went away; "it isn't when." He carried a blocking timber on the left shoulder and shored the post. He has the purse; a hundred and eighteen. He roped the three boxes for carrying on the night of the 277th, "whichever road they go up".
   172	
   173	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Her case stands as she made it and is "not by a line" altered. She has, received and receipted, **the flat (six rows, the sheets not counted, one row turned over once), the completion report, the leaf and the technician's sheet**, and her own exact copy of the sheet with a ruled box and *not read* in it. She has said that the word on the leaf is a title and not a name, that she has never met it in any stratum, and nothing more. She has said "More than four" and will not say how many more. She cannot read the index; it is now an office's index and not only the dead man's. She has not connected anything to anything. She keeps the lamp.
   174	
   175	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. He has spoken with Vastin for the first time (the doorway) and has given him his name. He has stopped his count at **forty-seven notches on the second wand (a hundred and forty-seven days)** and laid the wand on Karis's table. He went still at the date on the technician's sheet and said only "I have read it." He has taught nobody anything. He thinks the completion report may have been sent to Vastin on purpose and cannot tell. **The case is on him, shut.**
   176	
   177	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. A bench under the eave since the 272nd. She saw the bout and said nothing. She has not asked about the knee, and Vastin has offered it to nobody. **She has not read Cael.** She has shut her mouth three times on the same sentence. She did not sit on the stool. She does not know that Seln is Shadow's source.
   178	
   179	**Vastin.** No office, no seal, no rank; he left the seal in a tray "some months" ago and walked three hundred miles. **No age is stated.** A bad knee; raw hands; a left hand that will not lie flat. **No Iron Wall has been shown or named**; he held the ferry's stern strap with his hands and his back. He has handed over three things in his own order and holds Karis's receipt. He has said: that he holds no office and has no sanction; that the layer cannot be opened ("There is no key"); that the one paper which should name its maker cites a title and sends its reader to Treswick's lower archive; that nothing of his follows him and the Stair's rim is not his; that the pending paper is unchanged; why he did not take it to a council. He knows the six by name. **He does not know** the mechanism, what Cael carries, the instruments' behaviour in Cael's hand, Karis's case or the four sites (beyond hearing Brom say "four on the hide" and Lira name the Stair), who held the abstracts, or what is under the bar. He has not weighed the sheet's date. He has not read the flat's last row through, and nothing has been said of a directive or an objection. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. He has had nothing to do since noon.
   180	
   181	**Teague and his crew.** The wrist is unbound; he has tried it on nothing. He asked "When?" and was told "I don't know." His term holds without a day in it. The tall man drove the wedge at the post and grounded his spear for Lira; he, the bow and the older healer have said nothing to the six. Teague looked at Vastin's hands a stride longer than a crew looks, and said nothing. Nobody in his crew is named. He knows nothing of the mechanism or of what was said at the table.
   182	
   183	**Pike's book and the cloth.** **Eleven lines.** The season line's number still blank. **Eleventh on the new cloth**, painted on the 272nd. Vastin is "nothing yet" and is not entered; the boat's saving was "said". Oryn is on no slip and Pike has no column for her.
   184	
   185	**Objects and money.** **A hundred and eighteen marks in hand**, unchanged. The reserve sealed. Owed: **sixty yards of four-strand rope** to the ferryman (the cordage is on the western landing; his one hauling rope has two yarns gone). **The hurdle is paid** (woven on the 272nd, hung on the 276th). **The letter to Ephram is sent.** The three boxes are at the hearth's end, roped. Stake thirty-two has still never been driven.
   186	
   187	**The Quieting, as known.** Unchanged in the field. On paper: an office has surveyed the sites for six years by cord, has classed each under four signs, and has kept a narrow column and a total; its abstracts were held where nobody received them; the count is more than four.
   188	
   189	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before. The anomaly of the cord and the edges: the six. Karis's case: the six. What Vastin brought: the six and Vastin. Nobody has said who made the layer, or why, or what is running in it. Nobody has connected the sheet's date to anybody.
   190	
   191	**Words said aloud for the first time.** *Vastin* (Seln, at the landing). *Treswick* by Vastin, at noon, from the other side. On paper only, and said by nobody: the title on the leaf. Not said aloud by anybody in chapters 10–12: *west*.
   192	
   193	**Open threads.** A ruling to be given at the plank in the morning. A leaf that Cael has not touched. A date that stopped Seln. A bar with something under it. A figure under *Total* that does not agree with a count. A paper that came to a desk with no routing note. A sentence that a healer has swallowed three times. A knee that nobody has asked about. A man in a loft with a receipt and nothing to do. A rope on the wrong bank. A captain's term with no day in it. A question that Cael kept.
