    10	- Money: **a hundred and eighteen in hand, and it must still be a hundred and eighteen at the movement's end** (the map's cash spine goes 118 → 138 with the clearance slip on the 278th–279th). Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman, who will take a rope and no silver; one reed hurdle; a letter to Ephram for the first boat.
    11	- Pike: eleven lines; the season line's number blank on purpose; eleventh on the cloth.
