    24	- **Protected text:** every unit that BOOK_MAP §10 and the packet give whole for these chapters is in the manuscript word for word, once, as the plan now writes it, without its inline marks; a script of mine checked the exact strings. One `[[TIER-B]]` marker stands, on its own line, for the Compact date that the map leaves as a bracket inside the technician's sheet.
    25	- **Rhythm repair:** first drafts measured between 12.4 and 14.4 by chapter. Each chapter was re-composed by reading, by the same author in the same session, through individually written replacements of exact passages (joins of sentences that were one thought; a few long sentences divided; new passages where a scene ran short). No rule or script split or joined sentences at punctuation. A read-only listing of sentence lengths by the metrics tool's own splitter, and a small script that applied my hand-written replacements and refused any that did not match exactly once, lived in `state/movement-002/_w/`; the directory is deleted.
    26	- **No git command was run.** `BOOK_MAP.md`, `STATE_LEDGER.md`, the packets, `protected-patterns.txt`, chapters 1–6 and every other book's files are untouched. Nothing was written outside `manuscript/chapter-07.md`–`chapter-12.md` and `state/movement-002/`. `state/movement-002/audit-notes.md` appeared during the run; it is not mine and I did not open it.

