editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md-117-His own hand went to his coat that evening, on watch, and found a strap, and the corner of a lock, and nothing beside them. He let it lie there. He had thought that he might want the thing back by nightfall, as a man wants a tooth that has been drawn. He left it where he had put it, that night and the next.
