editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-54.md-219-He had perhaps a count. He did not spend it on the wall. A stone that stopped the thing once was only a stone, and it would go from him to the next weight that lay still, which was lying outside a wall with a healer coming to it.
