editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:27:"It rode on my mule for thirty rounds in a cover, and I looked at it at noon one day, at a stone, and left it where it was. It's done more across your knee than it ever did for me." Oryn did not put out a hand. "There's one in it. See that it stays in till it's wanted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md-28-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md-29-She looked along the five of them then, once. Her sum ran to the oxen ford on the hundred and twenty-fifth, three weeks after it had looked for her; then she said the thing that she had stopped the mule to say.
