editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-57.md-190-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-57.md-191-Cael waited until the bowls were empty. He had made up his mind to it on the road. A thing had been the healer's to hear before anybody, and she had heard it; and there were four people at that fire who had been told at a loft's ladder that it existed, and had asked him nothing since.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-57.md-192-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-57.md-193-"I owe the rest of you something. She's had it, as she set it, so it's free." He kept it short. "There's a place in me, under the breastbone, where nothing moves. All ten fragments go round it. I've read it three times, and it keeps. I don't know what it is, and I've been told to stop touching it."
