editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-187-"No. You've said." She set a strip of clean bark down on the scrubbed plank, and a pot of the hold's ink, and a pen cut from a goose quill. "There it is, all the same."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-188-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-189-Oryn looked at it after the door had shut.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-190-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:191:She did not keep a book. She had said so to the pale one across a fire: a healer who needs a page to know who is owed has stopped looking at them. She had never in thirty rounds set down a word about any person whom she had had her hands in. But those five were two days south, with a saddle between that would be shut by morning, and she could not look at them. There was a girl down there with an arm in a knot of hers, who had been told *first snow*; and by the feel of that sky she would be looking at it out of a window tomorrow.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-192-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-193-She could not read an arm from here. She had said as much in a yard, of a nearer gate than this.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-194-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-195-So the arm would wait until she could have it between her two hands, and that would not be before the thaw. The girl knew who was to say when. There was nothing in that to write.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-196-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-197-What was there, then? She went at it as she went along a bench, a person at a time, and told each the truth in a sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-198-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-199-The boy would be carrying her round. He had been told at a bar of iron that he was to have it and do nothing with it, and he had never learned to do nothing with a thing. He should hear how it stood.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-200-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:201:The small one had been in a loft when Oryn said that an old woman's knee did not care what was under a floor. She was a person who liked to know how a thing came out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-202-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-203-And there was what a round of three weeks had cost, which was the sum that all five of them would have been doing since a fork. It was not a kindness to tell them. It was a finding, and she gave people their findings.
