editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md-205-That left what she wanted, and she looked squarely at it, as she had on a road out of Oxhollow and under a cold stone. There was a calfskin with a strip of brass on it that pointed somewhere. Wherever it pointed, there would be an edge; and at the edge, somebody ought to be standing on the right side with her sleeves pushed up. She had said it in a loft, and she had been shown twice since what it was worth. And he was on the route, which meant one thing and no more.
