editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:7:## ENTRY — Movement 1, chapter 1 (Lowmarch lower inn; the hundred and thirty-first morning past the Line; after Oryn's letter and the Book 7 closing hearth scene; last ferry and rope-taking were day 130) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:18:| Oryn | Tide; Iron R4 provisional. Last located at Thornwater, with route work north next; grey jenny and thirty-foot three-strand rope with her. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:26:**Cael knows:** ten fragments with current costs/deployment notes; deployment since the Line is 27. The still place is a location under the breastbone, read three times, with all ten going round it and none through; `Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.` He has obeyed the no-touch order. Four sites lie on one map edge: Ring, Stair and Hall entered; fourth unentered, unnamed, undated and untested at 440 yards and two strides radius behind stake 34 repeated one per pace. The three entered sites stop live Arbiters while his already-dark Arbiter remains dark and his fragments answer. He has no Path; nobody knows why. He knows the kit's radius line, 41-kind index, stroke/bar and `third site confirmed on bearing`; Karis's `Someone made this pattern.` remains unanswered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:78:| 8 | Anchor-adjacent | unnamed hand | Perception absent at 14 feet, faint at 12, sure at 10. Purposeful contact unbinding at a knot is a deployment. A held point thins all other fragments. Two counted uses: Stair unbinding and Hall holding, once each way; Hall kerb trial not counted. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 16] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:83:**Deployment since the Line: 27.** Trace: ford 1; Ring 12; Tide/Oryn ridge 1; Stair 9; Hall 3; Tide/Oryn marsh 1. Self-readings and the Hall kerb trial are excluded. **Invent no new numeric ceilings. Preserve every numeric ceiling and bill fixed by canon.** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 16]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:122:- **Deployment since the Line: TWENTY-NINE.** Twenty-eight on the 140th (the Iron read on frozen ground beside a trapped calf) and twenty-nine on the 161st (the read on the river ice): both in earnest. Shed and meadow work is logged "Trials. Not counted". Anchor's counted uses stay at two; Shadow twice and sealed; no Tide use (asked of Lira and refused); no self-reading; Oryn does not read Cael.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:125:- **The stroke and bar** is on stakes thirty-two and thirty-four only. Karis cannot read the index and does not know it is a grade.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:142:- **Shale-backs, added to Book 7's account (flag):** a herd will lie up for the cold under a lee, on rock that it has scraped bare; it rises hind end first; a calf in fright makes a thin grinding cry and its plates stand on end; a herd roused by a calf lies down again when the calf is quiet; they will follow a strip of uncovered lichen at about thirty-eight to forty yards in the hour and will take lichen from a cap. Seventeen in this herd, four of them calves. The read was tried at 350, 200 and 60 yards and, in earnest, at a pace and a half: no answer was seen. Karis has entered both and calls neither a test.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:148:- **The kit as a tool (flag; as amended by the audit's five line fixes):** the cord is tarred hemp no thicker than a pencil, with a knot at every fifth stride and a brass eye whipped into one end; it is run out to its last knot, **the fourth**, and **"Four knots is a length"** (four five-stride intervals; no yardage is given anywhere); odd strides are taken with a notched slip of ash "a stride long by the dead man's reckoning". Karis cut a peg of peeled hazel to the stake's length. The inn yard, from the plank's left-hand post to a scratch on the stone trough by the gate: **"one length and four knots and two strides"**, forty-two; for Cael the slip laid once from the fourth knot leaves room for only half of it again. Karis measured the cord against the Ternhall brass on the 116th and again on the 170th: thirty-one lays "and a piece under half" to the first knot, unchanged, and the second, third and fourth knots the same.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:164:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: twenty-nine** (twenty-seven at entry; the read on frozen ground at the calf, the 140th; the read on river ice, the 161st). All ten tried in the cold term and written up as *The ten, by use*: Wind (the lock cannot be shortened, only placed), Ember (the burn), Shadow (held, not opened), Compression (both heels; ground worth a load), Pressure (seen coming; narrow and deep; comes back), Blade (short; the steel pays), the read (ground or air; a pace and a half; the eyes), Storm (one lane; ten counts; a fourth untried), Anchor (a point held to thirty; ten, twelve and fourteen feet), Tide (asked of Lira; told no; not used). Shadow used twice in all and shut. Anchor's counted uses still two. Tide: Oryn twice, himself three times, nobody else. **The still place** has not been read or touched. **The instruments:** on the 168th the kit's cord (four knots to a length) measured the inn yard at forty-two strides for Karis, Lira, Brom and Seln and at forty-one and a piece for him, three times; the Ternhall brass read a hair short in his hand and Hesk's a hair long; he has touched none of the three since; his ruling is *hold*; Oryn has been told and has no answer. Nobody has offered a cause. He lost to Teague's spear three to none (148th) and three to one (158th). He has entered Teague as the better captain. He has not ruled on Karis's case. He has written *West, and inside*. Body: sound; knuckles skinned on the 140th; near sight lost for an hour on the 140th and for an evening on the 161st, and back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:180:**Objects and money.** **A hundred and eighteen marks in hand** (96 − 20 for the cold stay; + 40 for the fence; + 5 for the roof; − 3 for the mule's shed). The reserve sealed and unopened. Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman, wanted with the first boat; one reed hurdle; a letter to Ephram. Stake thirty-two has still never been driven. Both brass edges are in their cloths.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:193:- **Cael and the fragments:** deployment is 29, not 27; the calf and river-ice reads are the two counted additions. Shadow remains exactly twice and sealed; Anchor's counted uses remain two; Tide was refused and unused; the still place remains untouched (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:225-229`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:239-243`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:211-217`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:189-201`). His near sight recovered after both read bills, and his day-140 knuckles are old minor damage by day 270 (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:217-225`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:191-209`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:205:**Movement 1 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Sol recheck of repair r1: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all four tracked passages RESOLVED against the source; no new tracking; every binding ruling above borne out by the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch3, the author's own "his Path" (of Teague) now reads "the Force"; ch6, Seln's sentence after Karis's protected speech now gives the asset-restriction as locked Book 6 ch58 states it — **the paper executes when an enrolled name is written in a book inside a district, and must be served within the hour** (not "a certificate inside the Line"). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report after the fixes. Final: 30,941 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (9 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment twenty-nine; day 270 at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:19:### Entry (Book 7 close; source Ch1 opens on the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:21:- **When/where:** Lowmarch, the hundred and thirty-first morning, after the Book 7 hearth scene at the lower inn. The first snow fell on day 129; the last ferry crossed and its lines were taken in on day 130; Oryn's letter arrived through a hand's depth of snow on day 131. Book 8 continues later that morning. The Book 8 count remains day 131 to day 308. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22:- **Cael:** nineteen. **There is no birthday in this book.** His own Arbiter woke at Kindling, its plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and it went dark; he has no Path. He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure (`the Bronze from Ardenmere` in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; sealed; used exactly twice, at Ring and Stair), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used once each way), Blade (Ephram), and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). Deployment since the Line: **twenty-seven**. **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted: read three times, told to Oryn and then described to the other four, untouched since Oryn ordered him to write it down and stop touching it. His ribs have been quiet since the morning of day 129. The living purse holds 96 marks. Open accounts are listed below; `nothing owed` is false. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:25:- **Letters/animals:** Hesk's brass and note and Oryn's bark have arrived. Letters to Hesk and Vell went west on the last ferry; Ephram's is deferred to the first boat of the thaw. The brown mule is with the five. Oryn has the grey jenny and the thirty-foot three-strand rope. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:34:- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:39:- **Vastin** is on the stick until the thirtieth day of Oryn's treatment month [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] ("Thirty's the month"). He walks with the five **unadmitted**. He has not asked to join and nobody has asked him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:55:3. **KEEP — The river is a road (161st); the kit on the table.** The cord is knotted at the fives, the stake is number thirty-two, plus the mallet and the field ledger with the radius line. The Stair's designation sits in an unreadable index above the stopped line "third site confirmed on bearing". Karis learns the kit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:86:34. **KEEP — The Span (304th).** First exchange: the watch's declaration is unanswered; Brom takes bolts on Iron. Teague goes through the middle (the barricade a body's length back) → **Force acquired** at a stride. Recoil: wrist, then elbow. The watch reforms. **Width:** "Nothing was gained inside" is entered first. "By count": five over stake thirty-four (Cael, Lira, Karis, the young one, Vastin), four on the shelf. They walk to the pinch. Eleven seconds. "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times." The watch goes east, unpursued. The win sentence (§10). The broad man goes over the sink's edge in the fourth second; Teague does not turn. Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers' nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's bill. **The Span** at noon: an arch on two piers over the sink, carvings on the piers' inner faces, the bearing "Through". Nothing happens on the crown. The thirteenth listens. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:91:39. **KEEP — The centre (307th dusk).** 506 strides. Rune turned on the floor at a hundred strides gives the same reading. The eyes are paid. **No edge, no seam.** "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made." He fit. It was not an accident. The third sentence goes unsaid. Oryn reads him at the line ("May I?"): "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He told nobody. The count. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:249:Running counts that must reconcile: **Lira's arm** "fifteen days" at 280, "twenty-five" at 290, "twenty-seven" at 292 and "thirty-three" at 298 (counting the 266th as day 1). **Karis's hand** is eight days old on the 298th. **Cash:** 96 → 76 → 116 → 118 → 138 → 136 → 130 → 127 → 123. **Oryn's route:** count "days past the end of her road" from the cairn on the 300th (§12 C3).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:259:| The ten (entry) | Taught as working inventory in M1, through practice, the ice road and the fence herd | Preserve the closed Book 7 rules: Iron air-or-body at Gold weight; Storm 10/10/12 laid and 11/11/13 clean, fourth untested; Shadow twice and sealed; Anchor 14/12/10 perception, contact unbinding and once-each-way counted use; Tide self/contact/clinical, ask and explicit yes outward. Deployment enters at 27. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 7] | Unchanged |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:261:| **11 · Iron-Wall-adjacent** | Acquired in the alley's quiet middle minute (M5) | Notice verbatim (§10). Deployment none | **Entered, not told**; the debt to Vastin stands |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:277:- The cold-term inventory and practice [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] (fragment names, costs, the seal, "deployment notes").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:360:12. **Fragment eleven (S12):** "Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. A plane, not a body: the ground told not to give. Distinct from the third — Iron-adjacent, the bed; this is not the bed hardened, this is a line drawn on it and kept. Engagement field: defensive; rooted. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:361:13. **Fragment twelve (S13):** "Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean — the direction a maker put in it; which mark bears, which is borne, which is nothing; whether a run sits or goes. Structure, not meaning: it will tell me a thing is an instruction and will not tell me what it instructs. Made things only. Not a river. Not a man. Costs the eyes, after. No use in a fight. Engagement field: inscriptive — the second field that is not a fight, after clinical; given, not taken. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Twelfth." Then: *He looked away. Kept.* *Not a man.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:362:14. **Fragment thirteen (S19):** "Force-adjacent. Teague. Partial. Bronze. Impulse along the line of the frame at contact: from the ground, through the man, out at the hand, and nothing to either side of the line. Needs a thing to push against — the barricade, the ground under the feet; nothing at a distance; nothing from the air. A body's length. The cost back along the same line, every time, at the place the line comes out. Engagement field: close; braced. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Thirteenth."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:371:22. **Departures (S24):** Teague: "The thaw's past," / "Noted," / "After the next thaw." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." / Oryn: "The day I have to." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." / Seln: "Six. Six and no mule. Nothing behind. Nothing beside." / "West," Cael said. / "West," said Brom, and picked up the box. / "Twenty-nine tomorrow," / "Thirty's the month," [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:384:- Teague and Pike (B7 edition `chapter-59.md:199,221–225`): `After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.` / `Noted.` / `I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:400:- **S10:** "Older than [UNBOUND]," / "I know that hand." / "Being believed — " … "It's the end of being able to be wrong." / "Give me a week." / "I'm sorry," / "Don't be sorry," Seln said. "Be nobody." Log: "Karis has been looking for this room her whole life. Cleon's been sitting in it for thirty years waiting for her. Vastin tried to open a door with his rank and nearly closed all of them — an Archmarshal's worth nothing here, which he's taking about as well as I took [SHATTERED]. Down here the stone's older than the Compact, so the Compact doesn't reach. First place inside walls I've ever stood where nobody can file me, and it's a hole under a city, and it's because everything down here is older than the machine that files. Karis says give her a week. I've got a box to carry and a promise to keep about a station upstairs. I can wait."
