editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-446-- **C9 — Lira's paper.** S8 calls it Lira's paper "on paper from a circuit". Canon (Book 5) makes her Iron R1 **formal at the Ostrand station**. **Edition:** "her registry paper", Iron, first rank, formal, carried unshown.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-447-- **C10 — The "first entry inside walls".** S14 calls the 292nd inventory "the first entry in the plain hand that had ever been made in a city", but daily log entries are written inside Treswick on the 282nd, 285th and 290th. **Edition:** it is the first *inventory* (the year's ledger form) written inside walls.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-448-- **C11 — "Tell Lira's family I said so"** (S24 letter to Hesk, kept by the final review). The referent is unclear: no Book 8 scene sets up Hesk carrying word to Lira's family. **Kept verbatim as source-fixed; owner to confirm intent** (it may be a callback the edition's earlier books should plant). [OWNER-pending #55]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:449:- **C12 — Office "six years" and the Kindling date.** "Six years" is the office's survey-record rounding. It is not paired with a numeric count since Cael's Kindling. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-450-- **C13 — Reader Standard repairs already made in the source.** Seln does not lie at the yard door (ruling 25). Consent is asked before every reading (S18 montage and Cael, S22, S24). **The edition carries both and adds no exception.** The source has no profanity and no gore to remove.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-451-- **C14 — Calendar of the leg.** STATE_RUNNING's first Ch19 note put the cairn on the 301st; the closed prose puts it on the 300th, with the crest on the 303rd. **Edition follows the prose** (§6).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-452-- **C15 — Rhythm (not canon).** The source runs a 21.3-word sentence mean, 19% of sentences at forty words or more, and a paragraph median of 51. The edition re-builds the sentences (§7.4), and Tier C wording stays verbatim.

