editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:8949:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-53.md:31:"The ruling says five weeks," she said. "That is the outside of it. The inside is in a section upon notices, which gives a district five days, and in the habits of a district clerk who has never in my time notified a date one day later than the code allowed him. Bracken went to the district hall on our first morning in the town, to look at the room where Brom would stand, and there is a board beside its door. He read on it that the station's frame-house was reserved for the registry's use on the last day of the year." Her voice was quite even. "It was written up before any ruling was given, and I want you to understand that there was nothing crooked in that. A prudent clerk books a frame when he sees that one may be wanted, exactly as Bracken books a coach, and he would have struck it off again without a thought if the seat had gone the other way."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:8955:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/manuscript/chapter-53.md:95:He had been sitting there a quarter of an hour, after the grey half, with two loaves from underneath and a twist of the fruit woman's apricots and nothing at all in his head, which was a thing he had been learning to do. The market was loud and slow around him. It was the first warm Saturday of the year, and people had come down to it who did not need anything, only to walk about in the sun and look at things and be seen looking. He had been watching them without meaning to. He had been watching the way a man in a brown coat came down the second row between the stalls, unhurried, reading the bread woman's high cracked lantern as if it were a notice, and he had thought, idly, *that man reads things the way they're written*. Then the man had turned out of the row toward the pie stall, and Cael had seen the set of his shoulders, and the brown coat had stopped mattering.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:8964:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-22.md:63:Cael did not need to be told what was under the hand. A square cream envelope with a dark red seal on it, unbroken, which had come up the hill twenty-three days ago and had not been opened since. Under it, the summons, the docket, the district's confirmation with *outcome anticipated* on it in a clerk's round hand, and a sitting on the last Fifth-day of the year at which three assessors and a sigil frame would almost certainly find Brom an Iron. His family's ledger had been waiting for that line since before he could lift a practice weight. In the second box was a grandmother at the head of a long table, and a word he had never once said in the same breath as *east*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:8967:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-27.md:25:*Three. Nothing served on this house since the eighth day of the year speaks of moving him anywhere.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:8970:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-47.md:203:*Deposited for safe keeping, the first day of the year's last month. Three boxes, roped. Depositor: K. Dellenmoor. Contents: the depositor's own papers. To be released to the depositor, or to her order.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:8975:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-55.md:41:The pen lay where Lira had left it. It was a plain steel pen in a dark holder, with the house's mark burned into the wood, and it had lain at that end of the counter for longer than Cael had troubled to notice. Bracken had said so on a landing two nights ago. *There is a pen on my counter. There has been one there since the fourth day of the year.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:8978:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-55.md:243:On the sill lay the enrollee's copy of the instrument. It had lain there, first leaf up, since the eighth day of the year: nineteen leaves on one side, thirty-seven paragraphs, three schedules, whose words he had counted on the first night as a man counts the guards on a wall. He left it where it lay, since it had been addressed to the house as much as to him, and the house could have it back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:8979:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-26.md:215:At the foot of the road the two coats stood in the lee of the wall, as they had stood every day of the year.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:8983:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-07.md:93:"Dated the first day of the year," said Bracken. "The morning of convocation. Somebody a week's road from here pressed that wax while the Chancellor stood on her platform telling this house to be what its papers say it is. I don't suppose they knew. I don't suppose it matters." He touched the second mark. "Served this morning. Seven days on a road the post does in three, at a walk, with three horses and a man in the middle who'd been told the pace. It wasn't sent to arrive. It was sent to be watched arriving. I watched it for a full minute from my window, and so did the gate, and so did the coats at the foot of the hill."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:8986:editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/manuscript/chapter-57.md:45:The old man was not there. Cael had not thought he would be. The old man stood in his gate at the top of the lane of yards on every day of the year, and whatever happened in the district went past him or did not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:9008:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-37.md:31:On this day of the year, the bluff had two lectures and a coursework deadline and nothing else at all. Nobody had marked this date in front of him since he left Fen Street, and somewhere along the road he had stopped being the kind of person who noticed. On the morning of his fifteenth he had written the date at the top of a page and gone on to the next line, and it had seemed to him then the right and grown-up thing to do.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:9012:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-11.md:67:She had borrowed Brom's docket out of his left inside pocket to copy its date, and Brom had stood in the annex doorway until she gave it back, which she did inside a quarter of an hour. She had the two dates on a slip, one above the other. Brom's panel, the last Fifth-day of the year, at the district seat in Ostrand. The seat's ruling, before the year's close, and there was only one Fifth-day in the year's last week.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:9013:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-11.md:85:The sittings went up on the covered walk's middle board that afternoon in Bracken's hand, under the house's one-line answer from the eighth day: *Sittings at the registry seat, Ostrand, on the seat's Fifth-days. First sitting: the sixth Fifth-day of the year.* Underneath it, smaller, Bracken had added a line of his own, which was a thing he never did on a public board. *The house will attend.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:9029:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-05.md:3:The eighth day of the year was a First-day, hot and still, and at the second bell Cael was on the covered walk with a book under his arm and nowhere in particular to be.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:9044:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-60.md:137:She unrolled the paper on the canvas and laid the brass along its top edge to hold it. It was a straightedge, an old one, which she had had from Ternhall. Cael knew the sheet before the firelight had found the whole of it, for it had hung on her reading-room wall on the first day of the year, and she had taken it down in the first week to make room for a code.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:9055:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-10.md:15:Then the rest, which was ordinary, as Karis had said. *The seat at Ostrand gives notice that it has convened formal proceedings upon the petition served on the eighth day of the year. The seat will sit on its Fifth-days, upon the schedule of the academic year, and will rule before the year's close. Counsel of record will confer with the seat's clerk upon the schedule on the twenty-fifth day. The first sitting will be held on the sixth Fifth-day of the year. Senior evaluators of the district will be called to the evaluation seat on a day to be notified.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:9093:rg -n -i \"registry year|compact year|day of the year|[0-9]+-[0-9]+|year [A-Z0-9]+[,.;:]|day [A-Z0-9]+[,.;:]\" editions/monroe-1.3/book-0{1,2,3,4,5,6,7}-*/manuscript editions/monroe-1.3/book-0{1,2,3,4,5,6,7}-*/state 2>/dev/null | head -n 400" in /Users/drive/fractured-path-monroe13
