editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-10.md:15:Then the rest, which was ordinary, as Karis had said. *The seat at Ostrand gives notice that it has convened formal proceedings upon the petition served on the eighth day of the year. The seat will sit on its Fifth-days, upon the schedule of the academic year, and will rule before the year's close. Counsel of record will confer with the seat's clerk upon the schedule on the twenty-fifth day. The first sitting will be held on the sixth Fifth-day of the year. Senior evaluators of the district will be called to the evaluation seat on a day to be notified.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/review-cold.md:63:1. **Location:** Chapter 12, technician's return, immediately after “Deep layer. Sequence initiated.” **Observed issue:** A bracketed `TIER-B` coordinator instruction remains in the manuscript where the protected Compact date should be. **Effect on the reader:** It breaks immersion at the most sensitive reveal and makes Seln's recognition impossible to evaluate from the page. **Proposed scope:** Replace only the placeholder with the approved protected date text, then recheck Seln's reaction and all date references for legibility and consistency; do not expand the explanation. **Strength to preserve:** The black brush-bar, Karis's “not read” notation, and Seln's silent recognition create excellent restrained suspense.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-05.md:89:It was a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it, and he had lived by the Compact's count his whole life before he had lived by the Line's for nine months, and a date was a date. He read the year. He read the day in it. He did the arithmetic, because a cataloguer does the arithmetic whether he wants the sum or not — that was all that a cataloguer was, a man who could not not count — and he had the sum before he had decided to have it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/audit-notes.md:18:  2. **The one standing marker, ch12 (the Compact date inside the technician's sheet).** Find the sheet's full protected wording in the source and how every earlier book of THIS edition (Books 1–7 manuscripts) writes a Compact date under the season-blind default (#35/#42/#48). Supply the exact replacement line, and any join needed at ch12:111–115. If the source date uses a month or season name, give the season-blind form the edition has already used for like dates and say where; flag it OWNER-pending if no precedent exists.
