+## 7. Names and source distance
+
+**Names.** There are no new edition proper nouns. The only apparently new capitalized expression is **The Architect**, and the prose correctly rules it a title rather than a name (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:65–79`; `BOOK_MAP.md:335`). The unnamed ferryman, broker, keeper, frame-shop mender, three road strangers, Teague's companions and Oryn's patients stay unnamed (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:135–167,213–243`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:205–255`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:143–147`).
+
+**Source distance.** The sweep probe reports 1,333 sentences, skeleton 2%, close 12%; chapters 10 and 11 are each 16% close (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:9–10`; manuscript spans `chapter-07.md:1–287` through `chapter-12.md:1–299`). With `SHOW=1`, 10 of 25 displayed close hits are protected or packet-quoted material: the stance/recognition/answer (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:171–183`), one doorway line and the B7-reconciled Karis line (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:19,149`), Cael's prompt and the close (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:99,105–109`), and the page (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:65`). The other 15 are short generic correspondences such as hands flat, brown coat, last sheet, or “nothing more to do”; none is a sustained unprotected source sentence (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:33,121,135`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:7,187,237`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:55,179,191,239`). The exact-overlap tool's nine runs are **9/9 allowed** after classing “Cael knew the stance before he knew the face” as packet-quoted rather than unprotected (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:9,69–76`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:47`). The elevated close score is therefore plan/protected document ordering plus generic table diction, not tracking narration. No source-distance rewrite is required beyond restoring/correcting protected units and removing the withheld original leaf.
