+10. `manuscript/chapter-10.md`
+   old: `"I thought so, and I read further, to be certain. It has been attempted, more than once, by the people whose business it is, with the best that they have. Nothing that they own will open it, and nothing that they own will read it. It is not locked against them. A lock is a thing that somebody has the fellow to." His hand closed on the board, slowly. "They sit upon it, and they have built the whole of their record on the top of it; and they could no more go into it than I could go into that hearthstone."`
