+1. `manuscript/chapter-08.md`
+   old: `He was the only man within a hundred miles who had ever been such an officer. He stood at the sill in a drover's coat of brown frieze, which was too short in the sleeve and smelled of sheep; he had bought it at the last market inside the Line, and had left a grey one on its hook. He had an ash stick, cut out of a hedge. He had a pack with one strap mended in cord. Under the pack, flat against his back, lay a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather, which he had carried so for three hundred miles less a few. Inside his coat, in a fold of oilcloth, there was a single leaf.`
+   new: `He was the only man within a hundred miles who had ever been such an officer. He stood at the sill in a drover's coat of brown frieze, which was too short in the sleeve and smelled of sheep; he had bought it at the last market inside the Line, and had left a grey one on its hook. He had an ash stick, cut out of a hedge. He had a pack with one strap mended in cord. Under the pack, flat against his back, lay a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather, which he had carried so for three hundred miles less a few. Inside his coat, in a fold of oilcloth, there was a single copied page.`
