+9. `manuscript/chapter-10.md`
+   old: `"I supposed what you suppose," Vastin went on. "I supposed that somebody above my desk kept the thing shut, and I went to look for the door that it was kept behind, meaning to learn who held the other half of the lock. There is an office that has the charge of the stations, and it keeps a schedule for the housing, and one for the plate, and one for the frame; it keeps a schedule for the function, which it maintains very well indeed. Below the function it has a single page. The page says that the layer is not to be opened, and it gives as its reason that it cannot be."`
+   new: `"I supposed what you suppose," Vastin went on. "I went looking for the door, meaning to learn who held the other half of the lock. The office's own page says that the layer is not to be opened, and gives as its reason that it cannot be."`
