+## 6. New canon minted
+
+Rulings correspond one-for-one to `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:125–142`.
+
+1. **Ferry rig — KEEP.** It is within the author's flood-landing ownership and creates no later conflict (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:5–23,45–61,151–153`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:57,73`).
+2. **First boat — KEEP.** Eight passengers, no goods, improvised repairs and the later foot crossing do not conflict with the map (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:29–33,127–143`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:129–145`).
+3. **Week's water/tent figures — KEEP.** They fit days 271–276 and the day-277 ferry (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:3–39`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:139–167`; `BOOK_MAP.md:217–218`).
+4. **Mule's stool — KEEP.** It pays the six-with-Oryn seam without making her join (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:53–71`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:27–39`).
+5. **Gate explanation — KEEP.** Its trigger agrees with locked Book 6 (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:75–117`; `book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-58.md:49–53`).
+6. **Oryn's Lowmarch bench — KEEP.** It is expressly author-owned and names no patient (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:135–183`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:45,73`).
+7. **New cloth — KEEP.** Teague first and the five held eleventh preserve the closed standing (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:187–211`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:202,205`).
+8. **Teague's salt/road term — KEEP, with Movement 3 placement open.** No contradiction; inherit the unresolved departure (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:213–243`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:255`).
+9. **Bout — KEEP.** It fulfills the packet exactly: arm speaks once, Lira does not stop, no fragment is used (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:3–135`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:46`).
+10. **Ephram letter — KEEP.** It pays the inherited letter and introduces no name (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:139–145`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:129–143`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:202`).
+11. **Vastin's arrival body/coat/stick/purse/loft — KEEP.** No age is stated and the knee carries forward to the cut (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:171–201,235–267`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:263–271`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:31`).
+12. **Vastin's road to the papers — AMEND.** Keep no key, citation, suppressed records, completion report, and inability to enter the archive; cut mender biography, frame repair, office schedules and failed-attempt history (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:143–173,189–225`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:65–68`). Exact fixes 5–11.
+13. **Flat — AMEND.** Keep the physical flat, six years, six rows, measures, *Total* and no printed total; remove the invented two-count disagreement and add the locked report's count of six (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:201–257`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:7–11`). Exact fixes 15–16.
+14. **Page — AMEND.** Keep a copied page, oilcloth and the protected line; cut the original leaf, binder holes, knife, cut-edge ethics and Blade prompt because the packet withholds the leaf (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:49–95`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:52,67`). Exact fixes 1, 12, 17–29, 31, 33–35 and 37–43.
+15. **Technician's sheet — AMEND.** Keep stock, technician form, bar and *not read*; cut the classification-event definition and leave the date owner-pending (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:101–151`; `BOOK_MAP.md:339,353`). Exact fixes 30 and 32.
+16. **Receipt — AMEND.** It must receipt a copied page and cannot say nobody examined material already read in part (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:157–175`). Exact fix 33.
+17. **Names given at the board — KEEP.** All six names already exist, and Vastin's decision not to write them is consistent with Book 6 (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:49–77`; `book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-40.md:267–273`).
+18. **Unnamed roles — KEEP.** No new proper name is minted (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:135–167`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:205–255`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:29–31`).
+
+## 7. Names and source distance
+
+**Names.** There are no new edition proper nouns. The only apparently new capitalized expression is **The Architect**, and the prose correctly rules it a title rather than a name (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:65–79`; `BOOK_MAP.md:335`). The unnamed ferryman, broker, keeper, frame-shop mender, three road strangers, Teague's companions and Oryn's patients stay unnamed (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:135–167,213–243`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:205–255`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:143–147`).
+
+**Source distance.** The sweep probe reports 1,333 sentences, skeleton 2%, close 12%; chapters 10 and 11 are each 16% close (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:9–10`; manuscript spans `chapter-07.md:1–287` through `chapter-12.md:1–299`). With `SHOW=1`, 10 of 25 displayed close hits are protected or packet-quoted material: the stance/recognition/answer (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:171–183`), one doorway line and the B7-reconciled Karis line (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:19,149`), Cael's prompt and the close (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:99,105–109`), and the page (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:65`). The other 15 are short generic correspondences such as hands flat, brown coat, last sheet, or “nothing more to do”; none is a sustained unprotected source sentence (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:33,121,135`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:7,187,237`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:55,179,191,239`). The exact-overlap tool's nine runs are **9/9 allowed** after classing “Cael knew the stance before he knew the face” as packet-quoted rather than unprotected (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:9,69–76`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:47`). The elevated close score is therefore plan/protected document ordering plus generic table diction, not tracking narration. No source-distance rewrite is required beyond restoring/correcting protected units and removing the withheld original leaf.
+
+## 8. Next-movement inheritance not already carried by Packet 003
+
+Packet 003 already carries day 278, the clearance slip, Vastin at the door end and not on the sheet, the silent drill, the cut, the spring, the date sum, the fork and days 279–281 (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:20–38`). Its author must additionally inherit:
+
+- **Paper custody and exact positions.** Karis holds the courier's flat, six taped rows, the completion report, Vastin's copied page, the technician's sheet, and her exact copy with the ruled box and *not read* (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:3–15,59–65,101–135,157–169`). At the close, the flat/report/original technician's sheet are under the lamp; the page is on oilcloth at the bare far end; Karis is comparing original and copy (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:223–227,263–265`). Vastin holds Karis's unsealed receipt inside the brown coat (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:157–175`). Seln's forty-seven-notch wand lies under the lamp beside the broker's sheet; he will cut no forty-eighth (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:251–255`).
+- **What each knows.** All six and Vastin have heard no key, the citation/title/place, suppressed survey records and the technician's visible line/bar (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:149–193`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:201–257`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:59–151`). Karis has not finished the records and cannot read the index or bar (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:223–253`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:129–135,285–289`). Seln has done an unexplained sum and said only “I have read it”; Cael does not know the sum (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:137–153`). Vastin does not know the integration mechanism, directive, objection, what Cael carries, or what lies under the bar (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:129–131`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:119–129`). Nobody connects the date to anyone (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:137–153`). Oryn has not read Cael and has not asked to read Vastin's knee (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:29–47`).
+- **Vastin's physical state and status.** Brown frieze coat, ash stick, bad knee, raw hands and a left hand that does not open flat; no age; no Iron Wall shown; not joined and has asked only for a bed (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:197–201`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:115–143,187–191`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:231–271`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:19–23`). He sleeps in the loft over the tap, up the keeper's stair, after beginning the climb fast and finishing slowly (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:263–271`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:193–219,297`).
+- **Bodies and equipment.** Lira's arm will be on day 13 out of wool on day 278, still slow and wet-aching; her ankle is sound in the large boot (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:127–151`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:3–5,71–135,147`). Brom's right shoulder remains in the older healer's knot (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:173–183`). The three boxes are roped tight for carrying with beckets out (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:243–249,281–283`). Seln's locked case remains shut (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:191–199`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:37`).
+- **Ferry and road state.** The ferry runs, but the stern strap is improvised from the stern line and the hauling rope has two yarns damaged; no wheels have crossed (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:151–153`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:129–145`). The sixty yards of cordage remain on the western bank (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:151–167`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:143–149`). Teague's forty sacks remain at the landing and his departure for the cold-road block is unresolved (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:213–243`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:255`).
+- **Ledger state.** It is the night before day 278; crew purse 118 marks; deployment thirty; ten fragments; Shadow still sealed after two prior uses; Anchor still two counted uses; Tide unused here; still place untouched (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:151–153`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:263–265`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:291–295`). Cael has not touched the page and has promised a daylight ruling at the plank with hands (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:223–241,267–299`).
