+
+**Compact-date ruling.** Books 4–5 retain protected named dates such as “the eleventh of Sowing”, “the nineteenth of Reaping” and “the twentieth of Reaping” (`book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-37.md:49,221`; `chapter-52.md:193`; `book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-13.md:127`) under OWNER #35. Season-blind Book 6 uses ordinal forms such as “the eighth day of the year”, “the first day of the year” and numbered First-/Fifth-days (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-05.md:3`; `chapter-07.md:93`; `chapter-10.md:15`), but **no Book 1–7 manuscript prints a Compact registry year-and-day date of this type**. There is therefore no value and no like-format precedent to reconcile. Fix 32 changes the misleading Tier-B marker to an explicit OWNER-PENDING marker. Once the owner supplies the exact registry year and day, the publishable three-line join must be:
+
+`*Deep layer. Sequence initiated — [OWNER-SUPPLIED COMPACT DATE].*\n\n*Unreadable. Not halted. Running. Correlated with classification event —*`
+
+The placeholder is not protected wording and cannot be ratified as final prose. No protected document is otherwise printed twice (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:105–109,239–245`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:65,111–133`).
