+3. `manuscript/chapter-10.md`
+   old: `"There is a thing that ought to be said, and I am the one of us who was trained to say it. In my old trade there is a grade of approach which begins exactly so. A man arrives with nothing: he has no seal, and no escort, and he limps. He has been wronged by the house that he comes from, and has left it; and he brings a gift, which is true, since only a true gift is ever opened." His hands were in his sleeves. "It is the best-made thing that the service has. I built two of them myself."`
+   new: `"There is a thing that ought to be said, and I am the one of us who was trained to say it. In my old trade there is a grade of approach which begins exactly so. A man arrives with nothing: he has no seal, and no escort, and he limps. He has been wronged by the house that he comes from, and has left it; and he brings a gift, which is true, since only a true gift is ever opened." His hands were in his sleeves.`
+
+4. `manuscript/chapter-10.md`
+   old: `"I know the grade," said Vastin. "I sat on the findings against three men who had worked it. Two of them had limps."`
+   new: `"I know the grade," said Vastin.`
