+15. `manuscript/chapter-11.md`
+   old: `"I shall not say tonight. I have not turned every sheet in six rows; and the clerk's figure and my own count do not agree, so that I have two numbers and no finding. He may have been counting visits, or instruments, or men, where I was counting places. A stroke in a column is a stroke, and the heading over this one is in the signs that I cannot read." She lifted her hand from the deal. "Both of them are more than four. That is what the paper says, and I shall say the rest when a sheet tells me."`
+   new: `"I shall not say tonight. I have not turned every sheet in six rows, and I have not checked what every group of signs names. A heading I cannot read is not a finding." She lifted her hand from the deal. "I shall say the rest when the sheets tell me."`
