+31. `manuscript/chapter-12.md`
+   old: `"I do not know. I held it to a window, and to a candle, and it has been laid on both sides." Vastin put one raw finger beside the bar, as Brom had put his beside the leaf. "This is the one thing on that sheet which I can read, and I had better tell you why. A clerk who withdraws a word strikes it once, with a pen, so that it can still be read beneath the stroke; the code requires that, and I taught it to every junior that I had. That is not a clerk's stroke. It is a brush. I have seen it on perhaps a dozen papers in forty years, and I never once saw initials beside it. It is laid on by somebody who has the authority to make a thing unsaid, and who does not care to be known for having used it."`
