+36. `manuscript/chapter-12.md`
+   old: `"You have had one bowl and half a loaf since yesterday. You held a boat this morning. You have stood at this table for the whole of a lamp, since you would not sit, and before that you sat on a stone trough for five hours with nothing to do, which I think was the hardest of them. You have handed over three things in the order that you meant to. I have them. I shall have them in the morning." She did not raise her voice. "There is nothing more for you to do tonight. You are to go up to your bed; and don't take the stairs fast."`
