   old: `"It is a title. It is not a name. A name is written as a name is; it does not take the article before it. A clerk writes *the registrar*, and *the keeper*, and he writes so of an office that somebody holds, and he does not trouble to say who held it." She drew breath. "I have read the Compact's paper from this year's forms back to the oldest charter that a certain house will let a person see. I have dated it by its stocks and by its seals, and I know four strata of it by the feel of the leaf. I have never met that word in any stratum: not as a title, or as a trade, or as a thing that anybody was ever called."`
