/bin/zsh -lc "rg -n 'fix(es)? [0-9]' editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/plan-audit.md" in /Users/drive/fractured-path-monroe13
 succeeded in 0ms:
21:- **REPAIR — extra sub-layer provenance.** The mender's training, damp-frame anecdote, service schedules and history of failed attempts add more than the four permitted facts (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:143–173` versus `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:65–68`). Retain only: unreachable/no key, citation, suppressed records, technician's line. Exact fixes 5–11 do that.
25:- **REPAIR — records.** The flat has six years, six rows, “More than four”, and the completion report as the last loose sheet (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:201–257`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:3–11`; `BOOK_MAP.md:62`). “Six rows” and “six years” do not themselves require that a row represent a site rather than a year; the next packet only requires a “second row” (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:32`). The plan's anomaly column contains *Total* (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:51`; `BOOK_MAP.md:62`), but the draft turns *Total* into a footer before a numeric figure (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:237–241`). Fixes 44–45 restore it as the repeated anomaly-column entry and remove the number. The disagreement between that invented figure and Karis's sign-group count is likewise not in the plan and would create a new Movement 3 mystery (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:241–253`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:95,150`); cut it by fix 15. The last sheet currently prints five names but omits the locked count of six (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:11` versus `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-43.md:47–53` and `chapter-40.md:231`); add it by fix 16. The Book 7 report's “No price paid” is not repeated here, but no contrary price is introduced (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-40.md:231`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:7–17`).
26:- **REPAIR — page/leaf identity.** The packet calls this document a page and expressly says “The leaf does not appear” (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:52,67`); the map reserves “the leaf” for the day-293 chamber reading (`BOOK_MAP.md:333,352`). The draft instead makes this an original leaf cut from a bound register (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:197`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:49–63,169`). Amend the carrier to Vastin's copied page without touching the protected line (fixes 1, 12, 17–29, 31, 33–35, 37–43 and 46).
28:- **PASS — fragments.** The only earnest fragment use is the Iron read of the landing bank (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:63–95,147–149`), logged as deployment thirty twice (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:263–265`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:291–295`). Pressure, Anchor and Wind are refused at the landing (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:63–71`); Wind and the read are refused in Lira's bout (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:13–15,95–99`); Tide is not used on Oryn's patients or Vastin (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:167–171`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:43–47`); Shadow is held and sealed (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:259–263`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:191–199`). Oryn does not read Cael (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:43–47`). The cut-page Blade prompt is unnecessary and disappears with fix 18.
40:2. **Compact-date marker — OWNER-PENDING, blocking final ratification.** The source does not print a value; it says only “and a date”, then describes a registry year and day (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md:97–101`). The map likewise has `[a Compact date]` (`BOOK_MAP.md:353`). No exact date can be restored without minting canon; see §5 and fix 30.
43:5. **“More than four” without a printed number — KEEP; CUT the number and disagreement.** The plan requires the qualitative line and *Total* as the anomaly-column entry, not a numeric footer or a clash of two counts (`BOOK_MAP.md:62`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:51`). The source also withholds the number because Karis has not checked it (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md:27–45`). After fixes 15 and 44–45, Movement 3 inherits no unexplained clerk/Karis mismatch.
48:10. **Orders/stairs — KEEP the walk-back mechanics; repair the speaker.** Vastin walks the order back twice, starts fast, stops and climbs slowly (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:193–219`), satisfying the Millrace sequence lock. Restore Oryn's source line by fix 36.
82:| Seln recognizes Vastin | **PARTIAL** | Manuscript `chapter-09.md:175` shortens and reorders source `chapter-02.md:9`. Restore the full source sentence by fix 2. |
94:| “More than four.” | **WHOLE, once** | Karis at `manuscript/chapter-11.md:245` matches source `chapter-03.md:41`; fix 15 prevents an unnecessary second paraphrase of the finding. |
97:| Vastin's page | **PROTECTED LINE WHOLE; carrier must be amended** | The set-apart line at `manuscript/chapter-12.md:65` matches source `chapter-03.md:69` and map `BOOK_MAP.md:352`, once. Do not change it. The surrounding original cut leaf violates `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:67`; fixes 1, 12, 17–29, 31, 33–35, 37–43 and 46 change only the non-protected carrier. |
122:12. **Vastin's road to the papers — AMEND.** Keep no key, citation, suppressed records, completion report, and inability to enter the archive; cut mender biography, frame repair, office schedules and failed-attempt history (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:143–173,189–225`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:65–68`). Exact fixes 5–11.
123:13. **Flat — AMEND.** Keep the physical flat, six years, six rows, measures, anomaly-column *Total* and no printed number; remove the invented numerical footer/two-count disagreement and add the locked report's count of six (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:201–257`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:7–11`). Exact fixes 15–16 and 44–45.
124:14. **Page — AMEND.** Keep a copied page, oilcloth and the protected line; cut the original leaf, binder holes, knife, cut-edge ethics and Blade prompt because the packet withholds the leaf (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:49–95`; `packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:52,67`). Exact fixes 1, 12, 17–29, 31, 33–35, 37–43 and 46.
125:15. **Technician's sheet — AMEND.** Keep stock, technician form, bar and *not read*; cut the classification-event definition and leave the date owner-pending (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:101–151`; `BOOK_MAP.md:339,353`). Exact fixes 30 and 32.
126:16. **Receipt — AMEND.** It must receipt a copied page and cannot say nobody examined material already read in part (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:157–175`). Exact fix 33.

